{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"agent_message","text":"Draft written and validated.\n\nSubmission: `update-01.json` (relative to the run draft directory), read-only structural validation returned `valid: true`.\n\nSummary of this increment:\n\n- **Behavior recorded** (`@b-lastindex-two-source`): a node's durable log end is the *max of two independently written values* — `getLastIndex`/`getLastEntry` (state.go 157-174) prefer `lastLogIndex` whenever it is `>= lastSnapshotIndex`, and the two halves are advanced by different ingest paths (`setLastLog` vs `setLastSnapshot`).\n- **Behavior recorded** (`@b-installsnap-state-updates`): `installSnapshot` (raft.go 1814-1953) sets `lastApplied` and `lastSnapshot`, restores configuration, and clears/compacts the log store, but never calls `setLastLog` and never truncates a pre-existing suffix above `req.LastLogIndex`.\n- **Investigation opened** (`@q-snapshot-over-longer-log`) with an explicit discriminator, and a registered gap for the reachability question.\n- **No defect asserted.** The interpretation is `unresolved` / `defect_claim: unresolved`, and the honest counterevidence is recorded: the obvious weaker variant is refuted by source — a fresh (empty-log) follower advertises exactly the snapshot index because of the `max(...)` in `getLastIndex`, and `compactLogsWithTrailing` deletes only up to `min(snapIdx, lastLogIdx-trailingLogs)`, so with the default `TrailingLogs` the follower normally retains the snapshot index and converges on the next `AppendEntries`.\n\nI did not run an experiment this turn, so the reachable witness was not produced with real producers; the draft states that limit explicitly rather than claiming the suspicion is confirmed.\n\nA note on the workspace: for native feedback I briefly copied the captured source into `draft/tmp/work` and built/ran the root test suite there; both that copy and the build cache were removed. The only pre-existing-suite failures were `socket: operation not permitted` on this shell's network tests (expected here, runnable in the controller's isolated executor), so no non-network test failure was observed."}}
